EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Lion_and_the_Lily_AnjouAndAquitaine_MicropedusOfBjornaerTheStarling" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Lion and the Lily - Micropedus of Bjornaer: The Starling"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Lion_and_the_Lily_Core_Ext"

    # Micropedus of Bjornaer: The Starling (Chapter Six: Anjou and Aquitaine, p76): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t692304ba42b27a0621e159 ^"Micropedus of Bjornaer: The Starling" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t705be3dc14c782e3c434fa ^"Nidi"]
            ^"Age" STRING "93 (Apparent age 60)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Determined +3, Fidgety +1"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 76
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The covenant’s name, which means starling, refers to Micropedus. He spends a great deal of time in his bird shape, and has difficulty transforming back into a human. A Twilight Scar has left him unable to change patches of his feathers into scalp hair when he takes human form, and he is finding the process slower and more painful as his Warping score increases.\n\nHis name, which means “small feet,” refers to a scar suffered in Twilight, so that his heartbeast looks more like a starling from folklore than from a forest. Many people think starlings lack feet entirely. Macropedius’s feet have become progressively smaller as he has aged. They are now child-sized, and he suspects that they will fall off entirely when he enters Final Twilight.\n\nMicropedus was the magus who had the idea that small covenants could exploit the uncharted spaces within towns. He has written extensively on his philosophy, and trained a few apprentices, but many of his Bjornaer sodales reject it. He is grooming Luna as his heir, although he was not her teacher.\n\nMicropedus is an Auram magus, skilled particularly in control of the weather. The covenant will miss him when he enters Final Twilight, because he sometimes uses his spells to break drought with rain and kill grain fungi with frost. His meddling, and the prosperity it bought to the area, is arguably responsible for the founding of a town so close to the covenant."
    }

}
